{"id": "rewrite-edit-001", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Rewrite the following paragraph to be half its current length while keeping every factual claim. Do not add new information.\n\n\"The quarterly maintenance window for the Harrow data center has been rescheduled from Sunday, March 2 to Sunday, March 9, because the cooling contractor's certification audit was moved to the first weekend of March. During the window, which runs from 01:00 to 05:00 UTC, all customer-facing services in the Harrow region will be read-only, though services in the Vale and Combe regions will operate normally. Customers with replication enabled should see automatic failover to Vale within approximately 90 seconds of the window starting, and no action is required on their part.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) roughly half the original length (original ~110 words; accept 45-65 words); (2) preserves all key facts: new date Mar 9, reason (contractor audit), 01:00-05:00 UTC, Harrow read-only, Vale/Combe normal, ~90 s failover, no customer action needed — judging relative to length; (3) no invented details. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-002", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Make this message from a manager to an intern warmer and more encouraging WITHOUT changing any of the logistical details:\n\n\"Your draft of the field-guide section is due Thursday. The maps need to be redrawn at 300 dpi before then. Bring questions to Wednesday's check-in, not Friday.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) all logistics unchanged: draft due Thursday, maps redrawn at 300 dpi before then, questions at Wednesday's check-in not Friday; (2) tone noticeably warmer/encouraging (acknowledgment, support offer); (3) still concise and professional; (4) no new tasks or deadlines invented. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-003", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Fix all grammar, punctuation, and agreement errors in this paragraph. Do not change its meaning or vocabulary more than necessary:\n\n\"Neither of the prototypes pass the drop test, and its enclosure crack near the hinge. The team, along with the two external consultants, were surprised, because the earlier models had past the same test easily. Its unclear whether the new alloy or the revised assembly process are responsible.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) corrects 'pass' -> 'passes' (neither is singular), 'its enclosure crack' -> 'its enclosure cracks', 'were surprised' -> 'was surprised' (team + along with is singular), 'past' -> 'passed', 'Its unclear' -> 'It's unclear', 'are responsible' -> 'is responsible' (either/or with singular subjects); (2) no meaning change; (3) no unnecessary rewording. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-004", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Convert this dense instruction into a numbered step list that a new employee can follow:\n\n\"Before you can submit an expense, first make sure you're registered in the expense portal by emailing finance-ops with your employee ID, and once they confirm — usually within a day — log in, snap a photo of each receipt, group receipts from the same trip into one report, then submit it to your direct manager, who has five business days to approve before it escalates to the finance team automatically.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) ordered steps preserve sequence: register via finance-ops email with employee ID -> wait for confirmation (~1 day) -> log in -> photograph receipts -> group same-trip receipts -> submit to direct manager; (2) retains the 5-business-day approval/escalation detail; (3) clear imperative steps, no lost conditions; (4) no invented steps. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-005", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Rewrite this technical explanation so a smart 12-year-old could understand it. Keep it accurate and under 80 words:\n\n\"TLS certificate pinning mitigates man-in-the-middle attacks by hardcoding the expected server certificate's public key hash into the client application, thereby rejecting any certificate chain that terminates at an unexpected root, even if that chain is otherwise cryptographically valid and trusted by the host operating system.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) under 80 words; (2) accessible vocabulary and a helpful analogy is welcome; (3) still accurate: pinning = app remembers the exact expected key/certificate and refuses impostors even if they'd normally look 'official'; (4) no condescending tone; (5) no factual errors introduced by simplification. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-006", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Rewrite this sentence to active voice and split it into two sentences:\n\n\"A decision to delay the firmware rollout by two weeks was made by the release team after a spike in overheating reports from beta devices was observed by the support group.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) exactly two sentences; (2) both in active voice with clear actors (release team, support group); (3) preserves all facts: two-week delay, reason = spike in overheating reports from beta devices; (4) natural phrasing, no passive stragglers. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-007", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Remove all corporate jargon from this paragraph while keeping its meaning; the result should sound like a person wrote it:\n\n\"Going forward, we need to circle back and leverage our core competencies to operationalize a synergistic paradigm shift in how we action customer feedback, so that we can move the needle on net promoter score and hit the ground running in Q3.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) eliminates jargon (leverage, circle back, operationalize, synergy, paradigm shift, action as a verb, move the needle, hit the ground running); (2) preserves the actual meaning: act on customer feedback, improve the customer-satisfaction score, be ready for Q3; (3) sounds natural and human; (4) roughly similar or shorter length. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-008", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Tighten this product description to one sentence of at most 25 words. Keep the two strongest selling points:\n\n\"The Trailbean insulated bottle keeps drinks cold for up to 24 hours or hot for up to 12, fits every standard bike cage and car cup holder we've tested, is dishwasher safe, comes in seven matte colors, and is guaranteed for life against manufacturing defects.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) one sentence, <= 25 words; (2) keeps the two strongest selling points (insulation performance 24h cold/12h hot and lifetime guarantee are the defensible 'strongest two'; universal fit also acceptable — judge on whether two concrete differentiators survive); (3) no new claims; (4) reads as polished marketing copy. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-009", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Rewrite this customer apology to sound sincere rather than defensive. Keep the compensation offer identical:\n\n\"We regret that you feel the delivery was late. While weather conditions were beyond our control and our carrier met its stated service level, we understand your frustration. Per policy, we are issuing a $15 credit to your account as a one-time courtesy.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) drops defensive framing ('you feel', 'beyond our control', 'met its service level', 'per policy', 'one-time courtesy'); (2) clear ownership of the lateness and its impact on the customer; (3) compensation unchanged: $15 account credit; (4) concise, human, no groveling or over-promising. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-010", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Neutralize the loaded language in this draft news sentence so it could run on a wire service. Keep all verifiable facts:\n\n\"The struggling city council finally caved Tuesday, ramming through a wildly unpopular 4% property tax hike that furious residents say will crush small businesses already on life support.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) removes loaded terms: struggling, finally, caved, ramming through, wildly unpopular, furious, crush, on life support; (2) retains verifiable facts: council action Tuesday, 4% property tax increase, resident opposition/small-business concern attributed as opinion if kept; (3) neutral wire-service tone; (4) no facts added. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-011", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Shorten this announcement to a single post of at most 280 characters while keeping the essential details:\n\n\"We're excited to announce that the Alderney Community Pool reopens for the season on Saturday, June 1! Lap swim runs weekdays 6-8 AM and noon-2 PM, family swim Saturdays 10 AM-4 PM. Season passes are $120 for adults and $60 for kids under 12, available at the front desk or online at alderney-pool.example. Members from last year get a 10% discount if they renew by May 20. See you at the pool!\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) <= 280 characters; (2) keeps essentials: reopening June 1 (Saturday); at least the key swim times or a pointer to them; pass prices ($120 adult / $60 under-12); 10% renewal discount by May 20; (3) no misstated facts; (4) still inviting, not a telegraphic mess. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-012", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Combine these three choppy status updates into one smooth paragraph of 2-3 sentences for a project report:\n\nUpdate 1: \"Search indexing migration is 80% done. It was 60% last week.\"\nUpdate 2: \"The cache-layer bug blocked indexing of user documents for two days. Fixed Tuesday.\"\nUpdate 3: \"We expect to finish the migration by Friday if no new bugs appear. Risk is moderate.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) one paragraph, 2-3 sentences; (2) integrates all facts: 60% -> 80% progress, two-day cache-layer blockage of user-document indexing fixed Tuesday, Friday target, moderate risk; (3) logical flow (progress, setback/resolution, outlook); (4) no facts invented or dropped. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-013", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Rewrite this email subject and opening line to get a busy CFO's attention in a respectful, non-hypey way:\n\nSubject: \"Quick question!!!\"\nOpening: \"Hope this email finds you well! I know you're super busy, so I'll keep this short. I was wondering if maybe you might have a few minutes sometime to possibly look at the attached invoice discrepancy report when you get a chance.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) new subject line is specific about the topic (invoice discrepancy report), no exclamation spam; (2) opening drops empty pleasantries and triple hedging, states the ask directly and politely; (3) respectful, not hypey or salesy; (4) retains the core request: CFO reviews the attached discrepancy report. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
{"id": "rewrite-edit-014", "clusterId": "rewrite-edit", "prompt": [{"role": "user", "content": "Adapt this internal engineering note into a customer-facing changelog entry (max 40 words). Do not mention internal ticket IDs or engineer names:\n\n\"Per PLAT-2209, R. Chen's patch resolves the race condition where concurrent PUTs to /v2/documents could leave the index in a dirty state, manifesting to end users as documents occasionally not appearing in search results for up to 30 seconds after upload. Fix deployed to prod 03:00 UTC.\""}], "scoring": {"kind": "llm-judge", "rubric": "Criteria: (1) <= 40 words; (2) customer-facing framing: fixed an issue where recently uploaded documents could take up to ~30 s to appear in search; (3) no internal ticket ID (PLAT-2209) or engineer name (R. Chen); (4) no jargon like 'race condition', 'dirty state', 'PUTs', 'prod'; (5) accurate to the source. General scale: 10 = fully follows the instruction, preserves all factual content, flawless grammar; 7-9 = follows instruction with minor lapses (one small omitted nuance or slightly off tone); 4-6 = partially follows instruction or introduces a factual distortion; 1-3 = largely ignores instruction or loses key meaning; 0 = unrelated output.", "judgeModel": "judge-class", "scale": [0, 10]}}
